From eb0a01c6779274562cb7166ab1ff10386cb2384f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 13:32:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: samsung: add the Exynos7870 CSIS receiver with DMA

The MIPI CSI-2 receiver of the Exynos7870 (CSIS v4.1) has a DMA engine
per virtual channel and can write frames to memory without the camera
ISP, whose firmware runs as a blob inside the vendor kernel. Use that
path only: the sensor is linked straight to a capture video node and
the frames come out raw.

Registers and sequence from the vendor fimc-is2 driver
(fimc-is-hw-csi-v4_0.[ch], fimc-is-device-csi_v2.c). The DMA address is
shadowed and latched at frame start, so the buffer programmed during
frame N is written in frame N+1; with nothing to program the DMA is
disabled and the frame dropped.

The memory layout of RAW10 is not documented: the first version stores
a 16-bit container per pixel and logs the DMA byte count of the first
frames, which is the measurement that settles it.

